    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The tracking data indicates a routine but evolving military posture across U.S. forces, with no immediate indications of heightened operational tempo. Multiple C17 and BE20 aircraft are transiting between theaters, suggesting sustained logistics and ISR support, while HAWK and TEX2 trainers in the southern U.S. reflect ongoing pilot training. Coastal regions show active SAR and patrol duties by H60 and A119 helicopters, and the USS Theodore Roosevelt&#39;s preparation for MQ-25 Stingray operations highlights the Navy&#39;s integration of unmanned systems into carrier operations. The return of USS Thomas Hudner to port after a multi-fleet deployment suggests a temporary lull in major naval operations, though the completion of PANAMAX 2026 exercises underscores sustained multinational engagement in the Western Hemisphere. Russian submarine net protection measures at Kamchatka and Black Sea bases indicate defensive preparations but do not correlate with immediate U.S. operational changes. Overall, the data suggests a stable military posture with long-term modernization efforts, such as drone control center integration, and no unusual patterns or strategic shifts detected.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
